  "worked_solution": "The center of the circle is located at the midpoint of the diameter. So, we can calculate the coordinates of the center using the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(h,k) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{3b+(-3b)}{2},\\frac{6b+(-2b)}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{0}{2},\\frac{4b}{2}) \\\\  & =(0,2b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius can be found by calculating the distance between the center $(0,2b)$ and a point on the circle, such as $A(3b,6b):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{{({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})}^{2}+{({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0-3b)^{2}+(2b-6b)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3b)^{2}+(-4b)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{b}^{2}+16{b}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25{b}^{2}} \\\\  & =5|b|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $b>0,$ we have that \n\n$$\nr=5|b|=5b.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the center of the circle is at $(0,2b)$ and the radius is $5b.$",
